      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Painful conditions are a common cause for visits to emergency departments. Appropriate therapy often consists of sedating medications followed by a period of observation that is beneficial in assessing their effect. The cause of abdominal pain is frequently elusive, requiring prolonged testing and re-examination. Observation is particularly beneficial in assessing this condition, while certain other painful conditions are not suitable for emergency observation because of the need for prolonged treatment."},
